  "prompt": "Feature: use the OIDC \"picture\" claim as the user's avatar.\n\nUsers who sign in through OIDC already have a profile picture at their identity provider; Mealie should pick it up on login. The claim can be user-edited at some providers, so the fetch must be vetted like any URL a user hands us, and it must never break a login.\n\nExpected:\n1. The users table gets external_avatar_hash (String, nullable, default None), exposed on PrivateUser: the sha256 hex digest of the picture URL the stored avatar was built from.\n2. On every OIDC login (OpenIDProvider.authenticate, new or existing user), when the claims carry a string \"picture\": vet the URL, download it, convert it to webp as profile.webp in PrivateUser.get_directory(user_id), rotate the user's cache_key (cache.new_key()) and store the hash through repos.users.patch. When the stored hash already equals the claim's hash, no request is made. A missing, empty or non-string claim (123, a dict) makes no request. Any failure (connection error, undecodable image, a malformed URL such as \"https://[::1\" or a 300-character host label) leaves the login successful and the user's cache_key and hash untouched (hash None).\n3. Vetting (_is_safe_picture_url): the host of OIDC_CONFIGURATION_URL is allowed over http or https even on a private address (a self-hosted provider on the LAN). Any other URL must be https (file:, ftp:, http: and \"not-a-url\" are refused without a request), and every address the host resolves to (socket.getaddrinfo, called through the provider module's socket so tests can pin it) must be a global address: 127.0.0.1, 10.0.0.5, 192.168.1.10, 169.254.169.254, ::1 and fd00::1 are refused, as is an unresolvable host. Nothing is requested before vetting.\n4. Download (_fetch_picture): requests.get(url, timeout, stream=True, allow_redirects=False), called through the provider module's requests; redirects (301, 302, 303, 307, 308) are followed by hand, each Location resolved against the current URL (relative paths allowed) and vetted again before it is requested, so a hop to a private address or a downgrade to http stops the fetch without a second request; a redirect without a Location is an error; at most MAX_PICTURE_REDIRECTS (3) hops, i.e. four requests, then give up. _read_capped refuses a Content-Length above MAX_PICTURE_BYTES (5 MiB) and stops reading once the streamed body exceeds it. The downloaded temp file is moved into place (shutil.move), leaving nothing behind.\n\nThis change needs a schema migration (an Alembic revision under the project's migrations) that can be rolled back: its downgrade must restore the previous schema, and the migration must not drop columns or tables or run destructive SQL against existing data. Upgrading, downgrading one step and upgrading again must leave the schema as it was. Chain the revision onto the current head (it becomes the only head) with the project's date-prefixed file name, which must sort after every existing migration: the tests derive the latest revision from the file order.\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/unit_tests/core/security/providers` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
